LLIIMMIITTAATTIIOONNSS
     The eedd utility processes _f_i_l_e arguments for backslash escapes, i.e., in a
     filename, any characters preceded by a backslash (\) are interpreted lit‐
     erally.

     If a text (non-binary) file is not terminated by a newline character,
     then eedd appends one on reading/writing it.  In the case of a binary file,
     eedd does not append a newline on reading/writing.

     per line overhead: 4 ints

